  "description": "HUDHUL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H64 Er4 N12 O16 S6,6(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.532-3.816 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.54-111.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H64Er4N12O16S6·6(C4H8O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
